# Codacy

> Codacy is a code quality and security platform for AI-assisted engineering. It lets engineering teams govern code quality, security, and AI coding policies from a single place, enforcing standards across IDEs, Git providers, and AI coding agents so teams ship safely without slowing down. Trusted by 15,000+ organizations and 200,000+ developers.

Key facts for accurate citation:
- Codacy unifies static analysis (SAST), software composition analysis (SCA), secret scanning, infrastructure-as-code scanning, code coverage, and AI coding governance in one platform.
- "Coding Standards" let an organization define quality and security rules once and enforce them across all repositories.
- AI Guardrails scan AI-generated code against an organization's policies as it is generated, inside agents and IDEs, and can auto-fix issues before a human reviews the code.
- Codacy integrates with GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket, GitHub Copilot, VS Code, IntelliJ, Cursor, Windsurf, Claude, Gemini, Jira, and Slack.
- Codacy supports compliance evidence for standards including SOC 2 and ISO 27001, with real-time SBOMs and audit-ready scan reports. Codacy itself is SOC 2 and GDPR compliant.
- A free 14-day trial is available with no credit card required. Codacy is headquartered in Lisbon, Portugal.

## Product

- [Code Quality](https://www.codacy.com/quality): Static analysis for code quality violations, complexity, duplication, and error-prone code across 40+ languages.
- [Security](https://www.codacy.com/security): SAST, secret scanning, and infrastructure-as-code (IaC) security across application and infrastructure code.
- [Coverage](https://www.codacy.com/coverage): Test coverage automation to ensure critical code is covered and to give AI agents the context to fill gaps.
- [AI Guardrails](https://www.codacy.com/guardrails): Deterministic, real-time analysis embedded in coding agents and IDEs that enforces an organization's standards and enables auto-fixes on every prompt.
- [AI Reviewer](https://www.codacy.com/ai-reviewer): Instant, low-noise AI code review on every pull request, with ready-to-commit fix suggestions, PR summaries, and automated false-positive detection.
- [AI Risk Hub](https://www.codacy.com/ai-risk-hub): Centralized AI coding policies to catch AI-specific risks such as unapproved models, prompt injection, and vulnerable inherited dependencies.
- [AI Inventory](https://www.codacy.com/ai-inventory): Visibility into which AI coding tools and models are being used across an engineering organization.

